@startuml
title Per radiograph: registration, then triangulation of the screws not in the CT
start
:Find exposed field (convex hull of textured region),\nreplace white collimation frame with field median;
:Detect nail in 2D (paired edges 9-14 mm apart,\nbright between them, robust line fit);
:Coarse search: lock projected nail axis on the line,\nrotation about nail +/-60 deg, lean, magnification, slide;
:Refine 5 candidates (Powell) at 4, 2, 1 mm pixels\nscore = gradient correlation of DRR vs radiograph\n+ penalty to annotated hints;
:Pass 2 with nail bend re-estimated from annotated bend marks;
note right: Camera per radiograph in CT frame
:Bundle adjustment over all radiographs:\nlag screw heads/tips + small per-image camera corrections;
:Anatomy constraint: head 1.5 mm outside tibial cortex,\ntip at most 3 mm beyond posterior cortex;
:Leave-one-date-out jackknife for error bars;
:Monte Carlo (400 samples) distance\nscrew surface to plafond articular surface;
stop
@enduml
